### ItemBagManager::Config ###
Each <Bag> maps one trigger to a bag Index. A bag is awarded through
exactly one of ItemIndex, MonsterClass, or SpecialValue - the other two
stay -1 on that entry.
  Index          Bag id. Must match the corresponding file's leading
                 number in Data/EventItemBag/ (e.g. Index="7" matches
                 "007 - ....txt"). Do not change for existing bags.
  ItemIndex      -1 = not used. Otherwise, the item index that triggers
                 this bag (e.g. opening item 7179 at a given ItemLevel).
  ItemLevel      -1 = any level. Only meaningful together with ItemIndex.
  MonsterClass   -1 = not used. Otherwise, the monster class whose kill
                 triggers this bag (bosses/events, e.g. Kundun, Selupan).
  SpecialValue   -1 = not used. Otherwise, an internal event code (see
                 eItemBagSpecialValue in ItemBagManager.h - Blood Castle/
                 Chaos Castle/Illusion Temple rank rewards, Crywolf,
                 Lucky Coin, Cherry Blossom Mix, Double Goer chests,
                 Imperial Guardian bosses, Online Lottery, Gift System...).
  DropInventory  0 = the bag's item is dropped on the ground, 1 = it is
                 given directly into the player's inventory.
  Name           Free-text label, for readability only (not read by
                 the loader).

STRICTLY NO COMMENTS INSIDE TAGS
-->

